Missing `strings` import in changes_compact.go. Also note: the CRDT compact endpoint is at `/v1/documents/{id}/crdt/compact` — my malformedChangesCompactPath checks "compact" at any i>0 — but `/v1/documents/{id}/crdt/compact` has "compact" at i=2 with segs[1]=="crdt" → my check returns true (malformed)! That would break the CRDT compact endpoint. I need to skip paths in the crdt namespace. Options: check `segs[1] == "changes"` requirement, i.e. only treat "compact" as the changes-compact keyword when segs[1]=="changes"... Actually better: only flag when the path looks like the changes-compact shape. Let me mirror the poll/replay approach but exclude crdt paths:

```go
for i, seg := range segs {
	if seg != "compact" || i == 0 {
		continue
	}
	// The CRDT namespace has its own guard; "compact" there is the CRDT
	// compaction keyword, not the change-log one.
	if i == 2 && segs[1] == "crdt" {
		continue
	}
	return !(len(segs) == 3 && segs[0] != "" && segs[1] == "changes")
}
```

Wait but what about `/v1/documents/x/crdt/compact/extra`? "compact" at i=2, segs[1]=="crdt" → skip → then malformedCRDTPath handles it (crdt at i=1, len(segs)!=3 → true → 400). Good.

What about `/v1/documents/x/changes/compact` — segs[1]=="changes", compact at i=2 → len==3, segs[0]!="" → valid. Good.

What about a document named "crdt"? `/v1/documents/crdt/changes/compact` — segs = [crdt, changes, compact], compact at i=2, segs[1]=="changes" → valid shape → not malformed. Good.

What about `/v1/documents/x/compact` (compact at i=1)? → return !(len==3 && ...) → len(segs)==2 → malformed → 400. Hmm — is that right? `/v1/documents/x/compact` isn't a registered path; without the guard it would hit... what? No pattern matches `/v1/documents/{id}/compact` — ServeMux: no pattern → 404 plain text? Actually there's no `/v1/documents/{rest...}` catch-all. So it'd be ServeMux's plain 404. The spec says extra path segments → 400. `/v1/documents/x/compact` — is that "多余路径段"? It's a single unknown segment. The poll/replay guards treat "poll"/"replay" in wrong positions as malformed (e.g. `/v1/documents/x/poll` → poll at i=1 → return !(len==3 && ...) → true → 400). So consistent: compact in wrong position → 400. Good.

Also add "strings" import. And register routes in server.go, and add the guard call in emptyIDGuard.

